RC3 is a top-secret research installation of the [[Org/Althane/The First House|First House]], buried under an unmarked office building in [[Geography/Althane/Oresk/Sarengrad|Sarengrad]]. Its front is a reception room labelled the Office for Regional Logistics, with a desk, potted plants and shelves of generic set-piece books; past it there are no offices at all, only a locked door with a small pad beside it. Entry runs the House's usual path: a passcard of any tier, a soul print, the fall of water called the Liar's Downfall, and an elevator down. A card opens only the floors at its own tier. The tiers run red, orange, yellow, green, blue, violet and ultraviolet, and the few ultraviolet cards open the whole facility. [[People/Althane/Karkov|Karkov]] holds one.

The floors grow stranger the deeper they go. On the first floor the Paranectural Cartography Division lies to the left of the elevator and the Department of Dimensional Correspondence to the right, a mail room of pneumatic tubing where five people hang fifteen feet in the air, mouths open and yellow light spilling out, all speaking the same words together. The Office of Symbiotic Interactions and the Bureau of Emotional Contagion lie between. Along the way, signs warn that this is a deja vu area, and that anyone who feels they have been there before is to report to a superior at once. The third floor's yellow tier holds the Department of Recursive Entities and the Office of Mnemonic Preservation.

The installation stands empty and mid-crisis. A klaxon sounds every few seconds and a voice in Oreskian repeats its warnings: a cognitive breakwater on the sixth floor, threshold manifestations on every floor, an unplanned architectural restructure in progress, and Contingency A12 in force to hold off a mnemonic breach. Hallways and ceilings rearrange themselves as they are walked, and the air carries a static at the back of the mind. Surviving personnel are called to Firebreak Gamma on the fifth floor, and the facility is sealed against any exit.
